  "conclusion": "SYN tracking installed before TCP birth preserves incoming state across later outgoing closure, including protected-born\u2192ordinary-Direct\u2192closed. A connection born before tracking still fails; a fresh reconnect after tracking succeeds. Existing outgoing replies do not create inbound permission, loopback does not acquire bypass state, and full release empties owned policy.",
  "limits": [
    "Only isolated IPv4 TCP PF mechanism; installed Mimo stays Direct. No installed lifecycle, SSH, Screen Sharing, IPv6 or UDP qualification.",
    "Captures show guest BPF observations; filter-hook position and absence of host capture prevent a blanket on-wire delivery/leakage claim. Client/server receipts support behavior.",
    "Production rule bytes are projected to dedicated fixture tuples; installed lifecycle and dynamic-self forwarding exclusion are not exercised here.",
    "The pretracking limitation is observed and not described as fixed.",
    "Neither general UDP/QUIC nor IPv6 nor route/interface migration is covered.",
    "Exact production bytes were compiled from source and narrowed to fixture tuples; candidate app lifecycle and dynamic-self local-address behavior require separate validation.",
    "Non-quick inbound pass permits a later administrator block to veto; arbitrary administrator rule ordering is not qualified."
  ]
